Dedicated to promoting African-centered holistic principles and providing a sacred support system, as a learning institute, where we advocate holistic alternatives; with a special focus on the health care needs of people of color.  We promote holistic lifestyle modalities that honor the whole person (mind, body, spirit) and encourage people to actively participate in their own health & wellness.

We are a support group for holistic health practitioners;
We offer continuing education to the holistic health community;
We are a holistic educational resource to the community at large;
We connect holistic health practitioners to the community in need of service;
We bring holistic health services to the community via various events and festivals;
We staff health & wellness for private, nonprofits,  community and governmental events

Tam Tam, Inc. is an immigrant-led, NYC-certified WBE delivering high-quality music and movement classes for children aged birth-8. We service early learning programs including daycare facilities, public and private preschools, 3K/4K programs, and Head Start Centers. We also provide family classes to parents/caregivers and their children, and after school programming for children ages 4-8. Our Music Together curriculum is research-based, internationally recognized, developmentally appropriate, and emphasizes adult involvement – including families and caregivers at home. Through singing, dancing, and percussion playing, our classes help children learn how to sing in tune, keep a beat, and participate with confidence in musical activities. The curriculum also raises the overall quality of a child's early education by supporting school readiness, family engagement, and classroom teacher professional development.

Key highlights:
(1) A highly-trained early childhood music specialist, educated in developmentally appropriate practice;
(2) On-going support for classroom teachers to incorporate music in daily activities, support classroom goals and enhance their curriculum;
(3) Play-based activities that support children's physical, language, cognitive, and social-emotional development;
(4) Family engagement via weekly home communications, special events, and the Music Together app;
(5) Promoting children’s physical, social, emotional and mental health with music education.
